# How to cite the Epistemic Record Format.
#
# `version` and `date-released` describe the tagged release. Both are
# placeholders until v0.9.0 is actually tagged; correct the date at tag time
# and bump both on every release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you cite this specification, please cite it as below."
title: "The Epistemic Record Format (ERF)"
abstract: >-
  A plain-text record format for bringing rigor to working research: the
  analysis, argumentation, and synthesis done in consulting, strategy, due
  diligence, and organizational decision-making, where conclusions rest on
  claims that no one can later trace, check, or stand behind.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bouet
    given-names: François
version: 0.9.0
date-released: "2026-08-26"
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/francois-b/epistemic-record-format"
url: "https://francois-b.github.io/epistemic-record-format/"
keywords:
  - specification
  - provenance
  - evidence
  - knowledge work
  - research data
